{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a set of sequences and a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" a dictionary keyed by them, both kept in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a trie (Fredkin, 1960): a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex paths spell the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keys. They answer the queries a hash set cannot: every key with a prefix"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"elements(withPrefix:)"},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" is O(1)), whether any key has one ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasPrefix(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the longest key that is a prefix of a query ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"longestPrefix(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Tries","","let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keys are any sequence of the symbol type and are stored as ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Symbol]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For text, the symbol","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type decides what a step is: ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trie<Character>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" steps by grapheme cluster, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by scalar, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trie<UInt8>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over ","type":"text"},{"code":"utf8","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by byte, the fastest of the three, because comparing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bytes is cheaper than comparing ","type":"text"},{"code":"Character","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s. When the symbols are ","type":"text"},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each vertex keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its children sorted, so iteration is in lexicographic order; otherwise children come in the order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they were added.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"},{"type":"text","text":" and a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary"},{"type":"text","text":" hold the same keys and answer the same queries,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the same names, in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): every chain of vertices with one child and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols, so there is a vertex per key and per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"branching point rather than per symbol. They suit keys with long shared prefixes, such as file"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paths or URLs, and build faster and in less memory than a trie of the same keys."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A trie’s shape converts to Grafluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and a radix tree’s to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"},{"type":"text","text":" of its vertices’ prefixes with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (import Grafluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trees"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module beside this one)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (Aho and Corasick, 1975) finds every occurrence of any of a set of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patterns in one pass over a text, in O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"z","type":"text"}]},{"text":") for ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":" symbols and ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"z"}]},{"text":" matches: a trie of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patterns with failure links. Its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is the automaton as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\").map(\\.patternIndex)   \/\/ [1, 0, 3]"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tries"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"externalID":"Tries","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"Tries"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tries over sequences of any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sets-of-sequences","title":"Sets of sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"]},{"anchor":"Dictionaries-keyed-by-sequences","title":"Dictionaries keyed by sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary"]},{"anchor":"Pattern-matching","title":"Pattern matching","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton"]},{"anchor":"Extended-Modules","generated":true,"title":"Extended Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees"]}],"references":{"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/statesView-swift.property":{"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.property","type":"topic","title":"statesView","abstract":[{"text":"The automaton’s states as a directed graph: a vertex per state, numbered from 0 for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"root, a goto edge from each state to each of its trie children, and a failure edge from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each state but the root to its failure state. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" tells the two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apart.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Symbol","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"statesView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">.","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV10StatesViewV","text":"StatesView","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTreeDictionary":{"title":"RadixTreeDictionary","abstract":[{"text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"chain of vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbols, each key’s vertex holding its value.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixTreeDictionary"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtreedictionary","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixTreeDictionary"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/TrieDictionary":{"title":"TrieDictionary","abstract":[{"text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"root-to-vertex paths spell the keys, each key’s vertex holding its value (Fredkin, 1960).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrieDictionary"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/triedictionary","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrieDictionary"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trees":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trees","kind":"symbol","title":"Trees","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/StatesView-swift.struct/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.struct\/symbol(ofedgeat:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"symbol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"ofEdgeAt","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The symbol a goto edge reads, or nil for a failure edge."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An automaton that finds every occurrence of every pattern of a set in one pass over a text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Aho and Corasick, 1975)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton","title":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trie":{"title":"Trie","abstract":[{"text":"A set of sequences kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths spell the keys (Fredkin, 1960).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Trie","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trie","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Trie","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries":{"title":"Tries","abstract":[{"text":"Tries over sequences of any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries","url":"\/documentation\/tries","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTree":{"title":"RadixTree","abstract":[{"text":"A set of sequences kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every chain of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixTree"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtree","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixTree"}]}}}